{:edb/db-before-t 2423 :edb/db-after-t 2424 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535736 50 #inst "2026-10-09T06:13:14.549Z" 13194139535736 true] [17592186068847 1020 #edb/ref 17592186363993 13194139535736 true] [17592186068848 1020 #edb/ref 17592186363998 13194139535736 true] [17592186068848 1020 #edb/ref 17592186364005 13194139535736 true] [17592186363993 1017 #edb/ref 17592186363994 13194139535736 true] [17592186363993 1017 #edb/ref 17592186363996 13194139535736 true] [17592186363993 1089 "q-348896" 13194139535736 true] [17592186363993 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535736 true] [17592186363993 1100 "Evaluate the following indefinite integral and fill in the missing coefficients.\n\n$\\int \\frac{7x+7}{(x+3)(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C$" 13194139535736 true] [17592186363993 1113 #uuid "fa3d60a4-4840-58c7-a2c5-661605cbc7a3" 13194139535736 true] [17592186363993 1145 "First, we note that the denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n(x+3)(x-4).\n$$\n\nWe convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7x+7}{(x+3)(x-4)} & =\\frac{A}{x+3}+\\frac{B}{x-4},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n7x+7=A(x-4)+B(x+3).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(4)+7 & =A(4-4)+B(4+3) \\\\ 35 & =7B \\\\ B & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-3,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(-3)+7 & =A(-3-4)+B(-3+3) \\\\ -14 & =-7A \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{7x+7}{(x+3)(x-4)}=\\frac{2}{x+3}+\\frac{5}{x-4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{7x+7}{(x+3)(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x+5\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+5\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535736 true] [17592186363994 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363995 13194139535736 true] [17592186363994 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535736 true] [17592186363994 1041 "field-1" 13194139535736 true] [17592186363994 1104 #edb/ref 17592186363995 13194139535736 true] [17592186363994 1110 #uuid "4c1b3a98-215a-5022-815e-c7b8f7564029" 13194139535736 true] [17592186363995 1034 "2" 13194139535736 true] [17592186363995 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535736 true] [17592186363995 1111 #uuid "7c3d8055-eede-5c29-97fe-82f360115b2d" 13194139535736 true] [17592186363996 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363997 13194139535736 true] [17592186363996 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535736 true] [17592186363996 1041 "field-2" 13194139535736 true] [17592186363996 1104 #edb/ref 17592186363997 13194139535736 true] [17592186363996 1110 #uuid "45841253-2a32-59e9-b236-9dd537fd51bc" 13194139535736 true] [17592186363997 1034 "5" 13194139535736 true] [17592186363997 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535736 true] [17592186363997 1111 #uuid "6d985051-c488-50a2-aafb-4f3c91bfb279" 13194139535736 true] [17592186363998 1017 #edb/ref 17592186363999 13194139535736 true] [17592186363998 1089 "q-49762" 13194139535736 true] [17592186363998 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535736 true] [17592186363998 1100 "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{2x+6}{{x}^{2}-4}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139535736 true] [17592186363998 1113 #uuid "17651bab-0045-573e-9f10-81a57a8387d2" 13194139535736 true] [17592186363998 1145 "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we note that a denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-4=(x-2)(x+2).\n$$\n\nSo the integrand can be converted into a sum of partial fractions,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+6}{{x}^{2}-4} & =\\frac{2x+6}{(x-2)(x+2)}=\\frac{A}{(x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(x-2)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n2x+6=A(x-2)+B(x+2).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(2)+6 & =A(2-2)+B(2+2) \\\\ 10 & =4B \\\\ B & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-2,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-2)+6 & =A(-2-2)+B(-2+2) \\\\ 2 & =-4A \\\\ A & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{2x+6}{{x}^{2}-4}=-\\frac{1}{2(x+2)}+\\frac{5}{2(x-2)}.\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x+6}{{x}^{2}-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-\\frac{1}{2(x+2)}+\\frac{5}{2(x-2)})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{5}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x-2)^{5}|-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x+6}{{x}^{2}-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x-2)^{5}|-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{(x-2)^{5}}{x+2}|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{2x+6}{{x}^{2}-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{(x-2)^{5}}{x+2}|{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|-\\frac{1}{3}|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|-{3}^{5}|) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{-1})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{5})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535736 true] [17592186363999 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364000 13194139535736 true] [17592186363999 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364001 13194139535736 true] [17592186363999 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364002 13194139535736 true] [17592186363999 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364003 13194139535736 true] [17592186363999 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364004 13194139535736 true] [17592186363999 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535736 true] [17592186363999 1041 "selection" 13194139535736 true] [17592186363999 1